result:
`ActionMenuButton2` is defined in the framework and used by five components in the patient chart, plus one test file that mocks it. Any behaviour change would affect those six chart files, and the framework's own mocks.

**Patient chart usages (best first)**

1. Clinical forms button, which calls `startVisitIfNeeded` before launching: @file:{openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-forms-app/src/clinical-form-action-button.component.tsx:1-29}
2. Order basket button, with a live `tagContent` count and `startVisitIfNeeded`: @file:{openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-orders-app/src/order-basket-action-button/order-basket-action-button.component.tsx:1-35}
3. Visit note button, with `startVisitIfNeeded`: @file:{openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-notes-app/src/visit-note-action-button.extension.tsx:1-28}
4. Task list launch button: @file:{openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-task-list-app/src/launch-button/task-list-launch-button.extension.tsx:1-20}
5. Patient lists button: @file:{openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-lists-app/src/action-button/patient-lists-action-button.extension.tsx:1-19}
6. Test that mocks the component and asserts it renders on tablet and desktop: @file:{openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-forms-app/src/clinical-form-action-button.test.tsx:8-15}

**Framework definition and exports**

- The component, its doc comment and its click behaviour (hide, restore or launch, plus `onBeforeWorkspaceLaunch`): @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/action-menu2/action-menu-button2.component.tsx:52-144}
- Re-export from the styleguide public API: @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/public.ts:35-35}
- Test mocks that the chart tests rely on: @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-framework/mock.tsx:119-119} and @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-framework/mock-jest.tsx:118-118}

The `onBeforeWorkspaceLaunch` callback is what the forms, orders and visit-note buttons depend on. If the framework changed when that callback runs, those three buttons are the most exposed.

Outside the chart, `openmrs-esm-patient-management` also uses `ActionMenuButton2` in its ward app. I left those out because the question is about the patient chart.

I could not look up the framework under the name `openmrs-esm-framework`, which Falkon does not recognise. The framework code is in `openmrs-esm-core`, which I searched by its full name, `github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core`. I did not modify any files.

